# Runtime dependencies of the extractor: the top-level pins (prompt 3 sections 6, 8
# and 12; docs/adr/0018-extractor-dependencies-and-sandbox-image.md).
# This is the input. The installable file is requirements.lock, compiled from it
# with every transitive dependency pinned and hashed (every file PyPI publishes
# for each version, so the same lock serves macOS arm64 and Linux amd64 and
# arm64). Regenerate it as docs/adr/0001-toolchain-and-monorepo.md describes,
# and install only from the lock, with --require-hashes.
#
# The extractor sandbox image (services/extractor/Dockerfile, target
# "extractor") installs this lock and nothing else.

# PDF: the native text layer, character boxes and hidden-text flags (no OCR,
# no PyMuPDF: AGPL). Apache-2.0 or BSD-3-Clause; bundles PDFium (BSD-3-Clause)
# with its third-party licences in the wheel.
pypdfium2==5.13.0
# XLSX: cached values and number formats, sheet and cell locators. MIT.
openpyxl==3.1.5
# XML: validating the draft IDS against the IDS 1.0 XSD (schemas/). BSD-3-Clause.
lxml==6.1.3

# Withheld, not installed (2026-09-25): ifcopenshell==0.8.5 and ifctester==0.8.5.
# Their PyPI wheels declare LGPL-3.0-or-later but ship no licence file, and the
# compiled IfcOpenShell library bundles CGAL packages that CGAL publishes under
# the GPL (3D Boolean operations on Nef polyhedra, polygon mesh processing,
# straight skeletons, 2D arrangements and Boolean set operations, AABB trees,
# box intersection, 2D triangulations, polyhedral surfaces). Prompt 3 section 8
# "Licences" and section 13 item 7: stop and ask. See ADR 0018.
